      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A diesel turbocharger uses high-velocity exhaust gases exiting the engine's cylinders to spin a turbine rotor. This-spinning turbine is connected by a shared shaft to a compressor wheel on the opposite end, which draws in fresh atmospheric air. As the compressor wheel spins, it forces extra air into the engine's intake manifold, increasing the amount of oxygen available for combustion. This allows the diesel engine to burn more fuel efficiently at higher pressures, resulting in greater power output without a larger engine size.",
